# Wave W17-P (Route 117): day elm — a field elm in bright open greens, broad-crowned over the flower fields with the highlight lifted clear of the turf, on day turf (ground baked in). Route 117’s own tree — brighter and broader than Route 116’s tiered echo pine (broadleaf field shade vs conifer hill ranks) and split from Route 104’s bed elm by crown register: the field elm shades worked land, the bed elm shades a road.
